+## Delivered source behavior
+
+The original `ProcessAsync_ProtectedHistoricalPayloadWithDestroyedKey_RedactsAndContinuesRehydration` test passed in a fresh source Debug build before this continuation changed code. The current Parties baseline already contained an in-memory JSON adaptation. This work narrows that adaptation to locally generated destroyed-profile redaction. Stored or provider-returned `json-redacted` cannot enter SDK replay, and an actor-history key failure cannot use the profile fallback. Full stored event metadata, exact tenant/domain/aggregate, sequence/checkpoint and required snapshot presence are checked before unprotection. Protection receives detached bytes, preserving stored envelopes.
+
+The shared EventStore retained source now rejects unsupported stored application metadata/serialization at both retained and excluded source positions before custody. It passes a detached payload to custody, preserving sealed source bytes even when a provider mutates its input. Strict SDK JSON intake, original sequence partition, source/authority rechecks, expiry, cancellation and purpose rules remain enforced.
