+The owner Local runner now passes an explicit repository source root to its test subprocess and restores the previous environment value in `finally`. Five existing UI architecture/privacy assertions therefore execute correctly when binaries reside outside the source repository. No required lane, class, assertion or analyzer was suppressed.
+
+## Executed policy and restore coverage
+
+The accepted policy remains `party-actor-retention-v1`, 365 fixed days from immutable binding-effective-at. New query tests establish/rebind at one shared boundary; a serialized restore returns the same old/new actor, version, interval and original source position before expiry. They exercise one tick before, at and after original exclusive expiry: restored readable bytes and optimistic synthetic custody cannot restart the clock or release the expired actor. A structurally complete profile-position partition still cannot replace missing predecessor transition/version proof.
+
+Actual shared retained-source tests exercise both expired-readable and destroyed-unreadable predecessor units followed by a live successor. The complete result remains unavailable; the reader does not decrypt the successor or manufacture an exclusion. A newly constructed reader with the same restored ciphertext/old readable key path consults current independent lifecycle and returns no history when that lifecycle denies. These are isolated source tests with synthetic custody; they do not qualify a backend or perform production backup/key restoration.
